WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO is about to start!

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.570
We're here at Cyclone Stadium with its continuous gusts!

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:14.080
Gassan Kunimitsu has made the first score!

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.630
<i>You were right, Kirino-senpai.</i>

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.160
<i>What?</i>

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.990
<i>I'm...</i>

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.000
<i>A Seed.</i>

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.340
<i>Just kidding. It was a joke.</i>

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:37.700
Why did he tell me he was a Seed?

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.100
What's he after?

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:41.810
Serves you right.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:43.850
Minamisawa...

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:45.560
Wait, Minamisawa!

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:33.600
Sorry.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:34.790
It's fine.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:35.960
We'll get the point back.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:38.670
Amagi-senpai.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.060
I overheard something.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:45.820
Kirino-senpai said you should've blocked that one just now.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.680
<i>Kirino</i> 's the one who messed up!

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.070
But Kirino-senpai is always saying during practice...

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:58.520
...that because Amagi-senpai is so slow, he always has to go through the trouble to cover for you.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:00.740
Kirino!

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:04.910
If you've got something to say, say it to my face!

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:06.960
But I don't...

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.220
Did Kariya tell you something?

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:12.120
Kariya has nothing to do with it!

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.630
Next time they come up on the offense, <i>I'll</i>  be the one to stop them!

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:19.050
I won't lose to the likes of you!

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.010
That guy...

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:24.020
Kirino.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.580
This isn't like you.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:29.240
The team's atmosphere has been different ever since Kariya joined,

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.550
but you can work with it, right?

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:34.850
Yeah.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:45.370
Kirino...

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:47.870
Get a hold of yourself.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.480
What do you think of Kariya?

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:52.880
What do I think?

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.020
Well, either way...

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:56.530
I'll let you handle those wind gusts.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:57.240
Okay.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:04.880
The match resumes!

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:07.870
Will Raimon be able to break out of the 1-0 score?

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:10.470
Primary formation!

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.510
Roger!

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.030
Tenma!

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.180
Okay!

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.910
I've figured out how they move.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.640
Soyokaze Step!

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.950
Matsukaze dodges the cyclones!

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:39.880
It seems he's completely figured out how to overcome the cyclones.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.170
Guys, obstruct his path!

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:43.710
Affirmative!

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.190
No!

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:07.850
Those two from Gassan Kunimitsu clearly knew that those cyclones were going to come in from the ceiling.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:14.620
When you're trying to keep an eye on the opponent, it's hard to track the pattern of the cyclones.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:18.150
It's as if Gassan Kunimitsu is performing combos with the cyclones!

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.000
The ball goes to Kai!

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:22.720
Claymore!

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:31.180
The ball remains in Gassan Kunimitsu's possession!

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:32.430
I'll stop them!

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:34.740
Amagi-san!

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.270
Stay out of the way!

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.400
Don't let Kariya's words brainwash you!

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.880
What's wrong with the defense?

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.940
It's Kirino and Kariya.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:48.960
It's coming.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:56.440
Secondary formation!

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:57.500
Roger!

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.400
Here comes the cyclones!

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.420
They've kicked the ball into the cyclone!

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.080
Again?

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.790
Defense, get the ball when it's loose!

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:13.390
Okay!

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:19.520
I can't get off his mark!

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.770
The cyclone disappears!

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.250
And the midfielder Kai jumps!

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.360
Get it in!

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:29.910
I'll get it!

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:36.620
Why, you...!

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.290
That was swift.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.330
I admire you despite being the enemy!

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.570
They complimented him again.

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:44.590
Is Kariya really a Seed after all?

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:47.390
Did you see Kariya's movement just now?

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:48.110
Yeah.

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:51.780
That's really impressive, to turn around from that position.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.050
Nishizono.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:54.850
You're up for the second half.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:55.770
Yes, sir!

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:01.160
Kariya makes a masterful cut!

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:02.230
Nice cut, Kariya!

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:06.000
That's the end of the first half!

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.240
Gassan Kunimitsu leads at the end of the first half at 1-0!

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:11.990
It's becoming a tough fight out there.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:15.500
We've got this nonsensical stadium to deal with too.

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:17.870
Gassan Kunimitsu is so unfair.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:19.960
It really is unfair.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:23.890
We can't tell how strong they really are when they're just using the cyclones.

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:28.970
But Gassan Kunimitsu definitely has the upper hand when it comes to strategies.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:33.600
They've demonstrated that through their combinations with the cyclones.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:34.590
Yeah.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.980
I can't believe even the stadium is our opponent...

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:42.480
This is reality.

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:45.040
Isn't this kind of soccer good enough?

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:47.400
As long as you do what Fifth Sector tells you to do,

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.260
you can graduate without stirring up any trouble, you see.

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.840
Do you really think that way?

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:54.880
Yeah, I do.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:58.930
So why do you guys keep playing when it only hurts for you?

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:00.660
It doesn't hurt.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:01.710
What?

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:02.970
Same goes for me!

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.070
We'll get our revenge in the second half!

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:07.430
Looks like <i>someone's</i>  getting worked up.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:08.800
How pointless.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.420
Kariya.

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:12.340
What's up?

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.550
Are you okay?

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:16.570
Kirino-senpai still thinks you're a Seed, doesn't he...

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:18.580
Oh, it doesn't bother me.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.840
Actually, it does.

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:27.510
Should I talk to Kirino-senpai and tell him that you're not a Seed?

00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:28.950
Naw, it's okay.

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:32.280
I'll just have to prove that through my plays.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.120
I see!

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.820
Okay, let's do our best in the second half too!

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:37.660
What a weird guy.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:40.710
He doesn't have the slightest doubt about me.

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:45.610
Kurumada is switching out with Shinsuke for the second half.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:46.440
Me?

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:53.890
To steal the ball back from Gassan Kunimitsu when they use the cyclones, we'll need Nishizono's jump power.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:54.630
Okay then.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.840
I'm leaving it up to you, Shinsuke!

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.600
Okay, I'll do my best!

00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.960
And Kirino.

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:00.890
Yes, sir!

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:02.720
You'll be on bench for the second half.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.220
Kirino is our key player for the defense.

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:08.690
You want <i>him</i>  on bench?

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:10.610
Got it, Kirino?

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:13.380
Yes, sir...

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.970
Then who will you switch in, Coach?

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:23.430
We'll fight the second half with these ten players.

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:24.660
Ten?

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.080
Only ten?

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.270
That's all.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.370
Everyone, get ready for the second half!

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:37.240
Good luck in the second half.

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:38.350
Thanks.

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:41.100
Coach, are you leaving Kariya in?

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:41.970
Yeah.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.100
Why?!

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:48.000
That matter aside, your plays in the first half carried a lot of frustration with them.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:51.000
That frustration threw the team out of order.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.010
But <i>he's</i>  the one throwing things out of order!

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:55.930
He might be a Seed!

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:57.370
Why do you think so?

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.150
He lies to people.

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:03.390
He's trying to break the team apart by spreading lies.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:05.900
Cool your head off.

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:10.420
Okay.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:20.610
Kirino-senpai, I don't think Kariya is a Seed.

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:23.770
He said he'd prove that through his plays.

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:26.760
Then he can go right ahead and do that.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.600
I'll be watching him right here.

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:32.850
I won't forgive him if he makes even the slightest suspicious move.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:37.430
What do you think after fighting your old home team?

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:39.030
They're my enemy.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.670
Nothing more and nothing less.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:43.410
All I have to do is win.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:46.320
Yes, their defeat is self-evident.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:48.770
Especially with their scattered defense.

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:50.100
They're full of openings.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:51.050
Aye.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:53.330
They're just crying for us to get goals in.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:56.990
Bring them down even harder in the second half.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:04.470
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:09.630
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:13.930
The second half is about to start.

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:19.130
Raimon has benched Kirino with no replacement and will start with only ten players!

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:21.480
Only ten?

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:23.780
They're belittling us.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.510
So they've benched one and challenge us with only ten.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.750
They must have some kind of plan.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:35.280
To challenge Gassan Kunimitsu with one less on your side...

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:36.630
The ultimate fool.

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:41.220
Gassan Kunimitsu kicks off the second half!

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:46.220
There it is!

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:50.700
Gassan Kunimitsu cleverly used these cyclones in the first half as well!

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:52.270
What will Raimon do?

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.590
We can't see them like this!

00:11:56.590 --> 00:12:00.920
Gassan Kunimitsu uses the cyclones like a wall to overpower Raimon!

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:03.990
They still have the advantage with using the cyclones!

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:07.240
I won't let you through!

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:14.250
It's Kariya's impressive mobility again!

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:18.920
Hunter's Net!

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:29.430
I'll get it!

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:35.720
Kariya has it again!

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:39.280
Raimon is keeping the ball in possession amongst its defense!

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:42.140
Oh, a cyclone is coming!

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:43.850
Kai, use the cyclone!

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:49.570
I've been watching you guys use the cyclones for quite a while now.

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:51.010
It's ours now!

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:54.580
What?

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:57.580
Kariya kicks the ball into the cyclone!

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:01.590
The cyclones in the second half are Raimon's eleventh player!

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:04.240
All right!

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:06.450
Tenma-kun, it's yours!

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:07.640
Got it!

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:10.480
Spiral Draw!

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.790
However could this be?! {yocchin ga futari iru?!}

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:19.200
Matsukaze uses a hissatsu technique!

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:21.630
He's jumped into the cyclone himself!

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:24.230
They've learned to use the cyclones to that extent?!

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:25.490
Tenma, go!

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:27.990
The eleventh player!

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:30.340
The cyclone moves freely!

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:35.790
No one knows when the ball or Matsukaze will come jumping out!

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:44.210
Mach Wind!

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:47.840
Matsukaze uses the cyclone to make a shoot!

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:56.850
Giant God Gigantes!

00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:58.760
It's mine!

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:00.320
A shoot chain?

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:07.950
Sidewinder!

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.260
Raimon ties the score!

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:18.710
Matsukaze assists Kurama!

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.920
The shoot chain using the power of the cyclone makes it in!

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:23.270
They did it!

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:25.490
Tenma-kun and Kurama-kun are both amazing!

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:27.760
Kurama-kun's first goal!

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.680
They tied...

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:33.570
Hmm.

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:35.670
All the more worth winning against.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.690
The coach has delivered his authorization.

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:42.480
Kariya!

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:46.000
That play earlier was so awesome!

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.300
Yours was too!

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:49.990
You've gotten really good at using the cyclones.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:53.500
Kirino-senpai threw the defense's balance off in the first half.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:56.110
Coach was right to bench him.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:02.420
Now it's obvious who's necessary for this team and who isn't.

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.420
Really?

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:08.630
No one can decide who isn't necessary.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:11.840
We're a team <i>because</i>  we have all sorts of people on it.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:15.690
Soccer must be feeling a bit lonely when you say that.

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:17.080
You two.

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:18.550
Get back into position.

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:19.130
Okay.

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:22.530
Lonely?

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:25.390
Why would soccer be lonely?

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:30.110
The score is a 1-1 tie!

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:33.320
Gassan Kunimitsu resumes the match with a kickoff!

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:37.300
The cyclones aren't coming!

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:40.090
The match has reached a new development!

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.820
Attack formation phantasmagoria!

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:44.440
Tactics Cycle!

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:45.410
Affirmative!

00:15:45.970 --> 00:15:47.430
Raimon, watch!

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:49.840
This is Gassan Kunimitsu's soccer!

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:51.210
What?

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:52.340
Hissatsu tactics?

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.350
They've changed the formation!

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.380
They're fast! Way too fast!

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:04.070
Gassan Kunimitsu's hissatsu tactics!

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:07.940
They're speeding up with back passes as they dive into Raimon's camp!

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:08.840
Stop them!

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:09.230
Okay!

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:15.240
Again... they changed it again!

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:16.920
The formation changes!

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:20.550
And this vertical line keeps speeding up!

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:26.940
Kariya!

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:29.220
Kariya, leave it to me!

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:31.630
I won't just let them push me over!

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:34.220
I'll get the ball from them no matter what!

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.380
What?

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:38.140
Would a Seed really go that far for Raimon?

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:42.130
Hunter's Net!

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:44.270
It's useless!

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:47.560
Kariya!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.740
Rocket Head!

00:16:56.270 --> 00:16:59.750
Gassan Kunimitsu scores again! It's 2-1!

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:01.030
Ow...

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:02.650
Kariya, you okay?

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:05.870
Got it yet, Raimon?

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:09.130
This should teach you how meaningless your fight is!

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:10.590
Minamisawa-san...

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.430
There it is again!

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:18.430
Gassan Kunimitsu's Tactics Cycle!

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:36.170
Guys!

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:38.440
Coach, is there any way against it?

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:40.990
Why don't you ask Kirino?

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:44.420
What did you see in those tactics just now?

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:51.600
In those tactics, when they move from a diamond formation into a single line, they leave a small opening.

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:57.060
When you're on the field, you tend to get caught by the fast movement, so it's hard to tell,

00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:59.710
but I could see through their timing.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.620
That's because I'm watching it back here.

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:07.430
Then Coach told Kirino to cool off his head so he could...?

00:18:07.430 --> 00:18:08.460
Yeah.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:12.820
Kirino needed to remind himself of his role as a defender.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:18.390
What the team has right now and what it still needs, that's what I wanted him to see.

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:24.010
From the defense position, he can observe the flow of the offense and figure out how to defend against it instantaneously.

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:27.460
He has the talent to analyze those things that quickly.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:29.250
I see!

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:32.880
This was all so Kirino could figure out a way to get past them!

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.960
So Kirino, how would you get past them?

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:39.920
What is it?

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:43.590
The key to get past them... is Kariya.

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:50.510
Kariya, with his extraordinary body balance, can quickly move from one point to the other, from any position.

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:52.150
Continue.

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:59.010
Kariya is the only one in Raimon right now who can do anything about the strong movements in Tactics Cycle.

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:04.050
If Kariya can grab a hold onto them during their movements, he can break the cycle.

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:06.320
But how will he know when?

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:09.310
I know the timing for him to break through.

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:11.380
I'll give the order!

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:17.600
Go, Kirino!

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:18.460
Yes, sir!

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:22.820
What's this? Raimon is bringing back the defender Kirino!

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:23.390
Kariya!

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:26.720
Do as I say for this.

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:29.790
Do you think I'll listen to you, Senpai?

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:30.930
You will.

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:33.350
If you really want to win, that is.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:37.510
This is something only you can do, so I'll put my trust in you.

00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:40.080
You'll break past those tactics for sure!

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:43.530
So you'll trust me. Awesome.

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.330
Kariya, please!

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:49.020
Yeah, we're counting on you and your soccer.

00:19:50.510 --> 00:19:51.740
What...

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:53.830
Stop putting pressure on me like that.

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:57.380
So now they're back with eleven players.

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:59.050
Stay on watch.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:01.090
There's definitely a reason why Kirino is back.

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:05.720
The match resumes with Raimon's throw-in!

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:11.310
Tactics Cycle!

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:13.890
Go!

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:18.590
Now, Kariya!

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:20.820
Go after #8 before they line up!

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:22.570
Kariya dives in!

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:25.030
Will he be able to break through Tactics Cycle?

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:30.870
I won't let you have it!

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.430
Kariya doesn't make it!

00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:34.370
The ball is in front of Minamisawa!

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:35.980
I won't let you!

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.710
There! Is that good enough for you?

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:40.770
All right!

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:41.550
Tenma!

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:42.760
Okay!

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:46.100
They broke past Tactics Cycle!

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:49.110
Kariya and Kirino make a magnificent combo play!

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:50.220
How could this be happening?

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:51.890
All right, looking good!

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:53.230
This'll finish it!

00:21:08.460 --> 00:21:11.170
Demon God Pegasus!

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.870
Go!

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:20.400
Giant God Gigantes!

00:22:53.920 --> 00:22:56.400
Remember, Minamisawa-senpai!

00:22:56.400 --> 00:22:59.890
The passionate feelings for soccer will stir up a new wind!

00:22:59.890 --> 00:23:04.600
Next on Inazuma Eleven GO, 
 Revive! Our Soccer!!

00:23:04.600 --> 00:23:06.190
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.260 --> 00:23:17.950
The Inazuma Eleven GO's proverb today is...

00:23:22.910 --> 00:23:27.240
No one is unnecessary. It's better to have all sorts of people!

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:27.940
That's all!
